# The test fixture corpus is a byte-exact contract, not source code.
#
# `edge/encoding/crlf.md` is uniformly CRLF and `edge/encoding/bom.md` carries a
# UTF-8 BOM on purpose; the vendored bundles are verbatim copies pinned to an
# upstream commit. Git's end-of-line normalization (core.autocrlf, text=auto)
# rewrites those bytes on checkout, which would break the very regressions the
# fixtures exist to guard -- and do it silently, on someone else's machine.
packages/okf-io/tests/fixtures/** -text
